			<div class="content" id="post-content-4853330">
									

<p>This was a solid scip concept. I think the writeup could be condensed and shortened; many of the details are thoughtful, but ultimately not very engaging. The Series I scips you reference in comments, the ones I remember most vividly, were very short. Strangely enough, your writeup for this SCP strikes me as far more realistic, in that it provides details that a containment specialist would want to review before engaging with the anomaly. My guess is that this realism weakened the piece; after all, most real-life containment procedures would be relatively boring documents.</p>
<p>The brief description of Foundation detective work was good worldbuilding. Unfortunately I think the dry, clinical tone restraint of the SCP format didn't serve that worldbuilding goal; it felt <em>too detailed</em> when I first read it, despite its brevity. After some reflection, I think the problem was actually a lack of space for narrative beats. I'd enjoy reading a tale that depicts the Foundation investigation with a little more vibrancy and drama.</p>

