<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there Undercover Fly. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>I see that you’ve revised the article a few times based on the other reviewers’ feedback. Unfortunately, my concerns boil down to two that I hope you can expand on / clarify:</p>
<p>1) Plot inconsistencies / lack of clarity. Why is this happening? It’s never hinted at / explained in your pitch besides mention of the Chaos Insurgency. More importantly, why is the majority of objects at the center “human corpses”, and how is it possible that they number in the billions? Just what exactly is happening? Why are the agents “blind, deaf and mute”? If so, how do they even use a computer? Similarly, why does the effect suddenly wear off and they die? Lastly, the Foundation not pursuing containment of the anomaly is not in line with their motto.</p>
<p>2) There still isn’t a coherent / developed narrative. The only line I can glimpse from your Central Narrative portion is an exploration log? Basically, the MTF goes incorporeal, communicate with the Foundation, and then they die? You need more than that, especially if you want to give your readers some semblance of answers as to what’s going on. Other suggestions might be to explain the origins of the anomaly, how/why the CI is involved and how exactly the Foundation goes about trying to contain this.</p>
<p>If you decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll take another look. Best of luck!</p>

