			<div class="content" id="post-content-4853274">
									

<p>I don't think this is a &quot;Safe&quot; SCP by current standards. Arguably it's Keter, because, as the author says above,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Rabbits can migrate, you miss one or two and they breed like, well, rabbits, so in a few years you've got the same problem again; dealing with this requires a large scale effort (you've got to comb every inch of half of Georgia), and the Foundation finds it easier to amnesticize ~20 people per year affected by this.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If the Foundation can't feasibly contain an anomaly, and constant vigilance and regular follow-up action is required in order to address instances' effects after-the-fact, that's Keter, right? I'm still learning, so I'm open to hearing explanations to the contrary.</p>

